## 📌 Project Overview

This repository documents **Week 03 — Project Module 1 (W3-PM1): Password Cracking with John the Ripper**, completed as part of the NetworkWalks Cybersecurity Internship practical work.

The exercise focused on password-security assessment of three supplied, password-protected PDF files. I extracted PDF-compatible hashes using the NetworkWalks Hash Calculator and used **John the Ripper (Jumbo)** on Kali Linux to perform dictionary-based password recovery with the RockYou wordlist.

The recovered results were verified using John the Ripper's `--show` option. Hash files, commands, results, and selected screenshots are organized in this module folder.

> **Module scope:** This folder documents W3-PM1 using John the Ripper. NetworkWalks Password Cracker web-tool activity should be documented separately if it is part of W3-PM2.

